Sval: Mozilla's tests load a test page where they loaded about:mozilla

Sval does not build about:mozilla or about:logo
(no-closed-about-pages.patch), so a test that opens one as an arbitrary page
waits for a load that never comes. These tests load an ordinary page from the mochitest server.

about:mozilla loads in the parent process, and two tests read its document
there. browser_iframe_gone_mid_download.js makes its iframe in the browser
window's own document, a parent-process document every test window has.
browser_swapDocShells.js reads the remote page's readyState through
SpecialPowers.spawn.

browser_splitview_integer_ids.js restores a split from session state alone,
and its restored tab loads about:about. A web page's tab is a node of Sval's
document, and SvalTabs.keepSplits ends a split of such tabs the document
does not hold (split-view spec §6.1), which races the test's check.

A test file has no chrome API to change the page it names, so the tests
are patched.

